{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790265200,"nonce":"1WFBq6himA4L626UJk05ux/sqXs=","title":"Python: a lambda whose body is a generator expression yields nothing","message":"Reproducer (main dea6d08b and later, ZYPY_LLVM=1 or not):\n\n    mk = lambda n: (n * k for k in range(3))\n    print(list(mk(2)))\n\nCPython prints [0, 2, 4]; zypy prints []. Through map the generator is also exhausted on the second read:\n\n    gs = list(map(lambda n: (n * k for k in range(3)), [1, 2]))\n    print([list(g) for g in gs])\n\nCPython prints [[0, 1, 2], [0, 2, 4]]; zypy prints [[], []] and then raises TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not iterable. A def returning the same generator expression is not affected.","files":null}]}